    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.surround\n\n### Description\n\nWhen using blockwise mode and `respect_selection_type`, multiline selections aren't properly highlighted\n\n### Neovim version\n\nNVIM v0.10.0-dev-2539+ga69c7206\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n```lua\r\n--- minimal.lua\r\nlocal path_package = vim.fn.stdpath(\"data\") .. \"/site/\"\r\nlocal mini_path = path_package .. \"pack/deps/start/mini.nvim\"\r\nif not vim.loop.fs_stat(mini_path) then\r\n  vim.cmd('echo \"Installing `mini.nvim`\" | redraw')\r\n  local clone_cmd = {\r\n    \"git\",\r\n    \"clone\",\r\n    \"--filter=blob:none\",\r\n    \"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim\",\r\n    mini_path,\r\n  }\r\n  vim.fn.system(clone_cmd)\r\n  vim.cmd(\"packadd mini.nvim | helptags ALL\")\r\n  vim.cmd('echo \"Installed `mini.nvim`\" | redraw')\r\nend\r\n\r\nrequire(\"mini.surround\").setup({\r\n  respect_selection_type = true,\r\n  mappings = { add = \"gza\" },\r\n})\r\n```\r\n3. Create file with this content:\r\n```\r\nline1\r\nlongline2\r\nline3\r\nlongerline4\r\nline5\r\n```\r\n4. `gg` go to first line\r\n5. `<c-q>` enter blockwise\r\n6. `G` select to last line\r\n7. `$` Select to end of lines\r\n8. `gza\"` Surround selection with \"\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nall lines are surrounded\r\n```\r\n\"line1\"\r\n\"longline2\"\r\n\"line3\"\r\n\"longerline4\"\r\n\"line5\"\r\n```\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nLines are surrounded at the last line's length\r\n```\r\n\"line1\"\r\n\"longl\"ine2\r\n\"line3\"\r\n\"longe\"rline4\r\n\"line5\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nNote that if this is done on the 4th line instead `longerline4`, then shorter lines are not even properly surrounded.\r\n```\r\n\"line1\r\n\"longline2\r\n\"line3\r\n\"longerline4\"\r\n```",
